solution:
The two group averages must be weighted by their group sizes, since every person contributes once to the population average. Write the numbers of women and men as \(11k\) and \(10k\), respectively, where \(k>0\). Their total ages are \(34(11k)\) and \(32(10k)\). Thus the population average is
\[
\frac{34(11k)+32(10k)}{11k+10k}
=\frac{374+320}{21}
=\frac{694}{21}
=\boxed{33\frac1{21}}.
\]
The average age is \(33\frac1{21}\) years, choice D.

